{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017AbEF68uvMwo43W6HQQyTd","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tname: session-protocol\n3\tdescription: Use when running a work-item (WI) or thread session in this template repo — how to read the plan, execute only the scoped work, pass the gates, write the session/WI log, and commit in this repo's style.\n4\tstacks: [any]\n5\tdomains: [any]\n6\tphases: [dev, gate, release]\n7\ttags: [session, improvement-plan, workflow, commit-style, wi]\n8\tscope: this-repo\n9\t---\n10\t\n11\t# Session protocol (this template repo)\n12\t\n13\tHow a WI/thread session runs here. The live homes: **`docs/status.md`** (what's\n14\tnext), **`docs/requirements/work-items.csv`** (the WI registry), and\n15\t**`docs/log.md`** (the session/gate record). This skill is the fast path; the\n16\tprocess masters (`PROCESS.md` / `PROCESS_OPTIONS.md`) win when they disagree. The\n17\tkit's design history — the old thread specs and the WI-1.x log — is archived at\n18\t`docs/archive/IMPROVEMENT_PLAN.md` (context, not a working surface).\n19\t\n20\t## 1. Read before doing\n21\t\n22\t- Read `CLAUDE.md` (governs editing the kit) and `AGENTS.md` (the pointer stub).\n23\t- Read `docs/status.md` (the working surface — what's next) and the scoped WI's\n24\t  row in `docs/requirements/work-items.csv`. The spec-of-record for a WI is what\n25\t  its row points at (an SR and/or a plan doc); older landed work is in the\n26\t  archived plan. **Do only the scoped work** — no unrelated edits.\n27\t- If a stub is being revived, find and link its earlier backlogged form (search\n28\t  `docs/archive/scratch.md` + the stub threads) so the resolution is traceable.\n29\t- **Check `git status` first.** Residue in the working tree is from an\n30\t  interrupted session; reconcile it against the open WI's spec / Done-when\n31\t  *before* new work — verify-and-commit what is complete, discard what is not\n32\t  part of the scope, and record which in the log. (The unattended loop surfaces\n33\t  this into the session prompt; the judgment is yours — it never auto-stashes.)\n34\t- **Treat a declared-policy change as a status-staleness event.** In the same\n35\t  sitting, grep `docs/status.md` and `docs/run-state` for pause/stop/approval\n36\t  language predicated on the old `gate-policy`, `push-policy`, `review-policy`,\n37\t  or `guardrails-policy` value; point to the policy file instead of paraphrasing it.\n38\t\n39\t## 2. Respect the constraints\n40\t\n41\t- **Byte budgets** on `AGENTS.template.md` (10,000) and `PROCESS.md` — see the\n42\t  `byte-budget-guard` skill. Push expansion to `PROCESS_OPTIONS.md` /\n43\t  `ADOPTING.md` / `EXAMPLE.md`.\n44\t- **Stdlib-only, cross-platform** kit scripts (Python 3.8+, Windows + POSIX).\n45\t- **Single source of truth:** state a fact once and link to it; don't paraphrase\n46\t  a rule into five files.\n47\t\n48\t## 3. End green (gates)\n49\t\n50\tRun the real checks and paste the real output — never a green you didn't produce:\n51\t\n52\t```\n53\tpython -m pytest -q -n auto -m smoke\n54\tpython project-trajectory/scripts/check_docs.py --root . --stale\n55\t```\n56\t\n57\tBoth must pass before **each** commit — this is the **commit bar**. `-m smoke`\n58\tis the fast per-commit tier (WI-122: ~47 s / 531 cases vs ~66 s / 684 for the\n59\tfull suite, both `-n auto` — the declared stack.ini command, WI-075). Tiering\n60\tis opt-out: smoke drops only the heavy end-to-end modules\n61\t(`tests/conftest.py` `SLOW_MODULES` — full hook/gate/scaffold runs the commit\n62\thook and the gate re-exercise anyway), so a **new test is in the bar by\n63\tdefault**. Run the **full** unfiltered suite (`pytest -q -n auto`) before\n64\tclaiming a slice/campaign done, at close, and after a broad script change. The\n65\tfull `check.py --gate <gate>` is the **gate bar** (unfiltered suite + coverage):\n66\tit belongs to gate advancement, campaign close, and CI, not to each\n67\tmid-campaign slice; `--jobs 0` runs its independent steps concurrently. A per-WI\n68\tslice inside a campaign ends at the commit bar (PROCESS_OPTIONS.md, \"Campaign\n69\truling\"). New behavior needs new tests\n70\t(`tests/`); update `test_bootstrap.py` file lists and `README.md` kit-contents /\n71\t`bootstrap.py` `MAPPING` when the scaffold surface changes.\n72\t\n73\t## 4. Record the work\n74\t\n75\t- Set the WI's row in `docs/requirements/work-items.csv` to `done` with its\n76\t  deliverable, and add a session entry to `docs/log.md`: one-line summary,\n77\t  deliverables, **deviations from spec**, **byte deltas on budgeted files**, and\n78\t  the `pytest -q` totals (match the style already there).\n79\t- Update `docs/status.md` to point at what's next; don't leave a stale \"next\".\n80\t- Where the unattended coordinator is in use, maintain `docs/next-wi` (the next\n81\t  WI id — or a `;`-joined ordered batch of independent, off-spine WIs, which one\n82\t  BUILD session executes in order under ONE review round; dev-slice batching,\n83\t  WI-133) alongside `status.md`'s Next action, so a managed BUILD session honors\n84\t  the `BuildTier` pin — strongest member wins in a batch (process-options.md\n85\t  \"Unattended operation\").\n86\t\n87\t## 5. Commit in this repo's style\n88\t\n89\t- **Logical commits** — one per deliverable/thread, message\n90\t  `WI-<n>: <imperative subject>` then a body explaining the *why* and any\n91\t  deviation (see recent `git log`).\n92\t- **Attribution footers are fine here** — add `Co-Authored-By:` as usual (this\n93\t  repo is not anonymous). Omit them only in a privacy-restricted / anonymous repo,\n94\t  where a tool trailer is itself a leak (process-options.md \"Commit identity &\n95\t  privacy\").\n96\t- **Do not push** unless explicitly asked; branch is whatever the plan header's\n97\t  **Branch:** line names.\n98\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"aa2aa970-11cb-4b2d-8aaa-2b2993dea9b3","uuid":"414a9c90-845e-4dba-ae99-b237ababd90e","timesta